{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3566","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3566","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3566\",\"parent_revision\":\"ac9d9d9b051e4fe02ab588683b976d28bedf3a09f13b2bea23060eff5b79276d\",\"root_revision\":\"ac9d9d9b051e4fe02ab588683b976d28bedf3a09f13b2bea23060eff5b79276d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-14\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Goal**: a skill can ask the backlog \\\"which items are in progress?\\\" and get the same answer on every configured backend.\\n\\n**Observed behavior**: `backlog_list(status=\\\"in-progress\\\")` returns no in-progress items on any backend. The status filter compares the requested value with each item's derived status by exact string match, and each backend reports an in-progress item differently:\\n\\n| Backend | How \\\"in progress\\\" is written | Value the status filter compares | Matches `in-progress` |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| GitHub | issue label `status:in-progress` | the `status:`-prefixed label | no; only `status:in-progress` matches |\\n| Beads | native status column, set by `bd update --claim` | native `in_progress` | no; only `in_progress` matches |\\n| SQLite | a tag on the issue row; the `status` column stays `open` | the `status` column (`open` or `closed`) | never |\\n| Memory | nothing is written | the issue state (`open` or `closed`) | never |\\n\\n**Reproduction**:\\n1. Put an item in progress through `backlog_update(status=\\\"in-progress\\\")` on each backend.\\n2. Call `backlog_list(status=\\\"in-progress\\\")`.\\n3. Observe that the item is absent from the result on every backend.\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- GitHub: `backlog_core/gh_client.py` batch status fetch builds the status from `status:`-prefixed labels; `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` filters with `status=\\\"status:in-progress\\\"`, and the `backlog_list` MCP parameter documents `'status:in-progress'` as its example.\\n- Beads: `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` `list_work_items` sets the item status to the native value; `tests_backlog/test_beads_backend.py` asserts `item.status == \\\"in_progress\\\"`. Beads status is a native column and beads labels are unrelated free-form strings (`docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/02-beads-data-model.md` \u00a72 and \u00a76).\\n- SQLite: `backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py` `apply_status_in_progress` tags the row; `batch_fetch_statuses` returns the `status` column.\\n- Memory: `backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py` `apply_status_in_progress` is a no-op; `batch_fetch_statuses` returns the issue state.\\n- Filter: `backlog_core/operations.py` `_filter_open_items` compares `_item_derived_status(item) == status`.\\n\\n**Impact**: no skill can find in-progress work in a backend-neutral way. `work-backlog-item`'s quick workflow searched with `status=\\\"in-progress\\\"`, matched nothing on any backend, and had its in-progress integration step removed in #3427 rather than encode one backend's spelling.\\n\\n**Expected behavior**: one status value names \\\"in progress\\\" and matches in-progress items on GitHub, Beads, SQLite and memory.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - session observation while fixing review findings on #3427\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-14\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3761c50276512d1be9969d8c1c855b926c0550e58754be1ba1f27b5d1f56d5bd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUeTA_w\"}"}